      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_3",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s3"
      },
      "text": "We have been tracking Roaming Mantis since 2018, and published five blog posts about this campaign:",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s4"
      },
      "text": "It’s been a while since the last blog post, but we’ve observed some new activities by Roaming Mantis in 2021, and some changes in the Android Trojan Wroba.g (or Wroba.o, a.k.a Moqhao, XLoader) that’s mainly used in this campaign.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "Smishing alerts on German and French websites Typically, the smishing messages contain a very short description and a URL to a landing page.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s2"
      },
      "text": "Territories affected by Trojan-Dropper.AndroidOS.Wroba.g and Trojan- Dropper.AndroidOS.Wroba.o (download) We’d also like to point out some very interesting data on Roaming Mantis landing page statistics published on Internet Week 2021 and Github by @ninoseki, an independent security expert based in Japan.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_9",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s3"
      },
      "text": "The data shows the number of downloaded APK files, landing page domains, and IP addresses located in the seven regions targeted most by Roaming Mantis using Wroba.g/Wroba.o on a particular day in September 2021.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_10",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s4"
      },
      "text": "The number of downloaded APK files and IPs/domains of landing pages The following table is a ranking based on the number of APK file downloads.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_12",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s1"
      },
      "text": "Anti-researcher tricks in the landing page Throughout 2020 and 2021, the criminal group behind Roaming Mantis made use of various obfuscation techniques in the landing page script in order to evade detection.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_15",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s1"
      },
      "text": "Technical analysis: loader module of Wroba.g/Wroba.o We performed in-depth analysis of Wroba.g/Wroba.o samples and observed several modifications in the loader module and payload, using kuronekoyamato.apk as an example.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_23",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s4"
      },
      "text": "Technical analysis: payload of Wroba.g/Wroba.o Regarding the updates to the Wroba.g/Wroba.o payload, Kaspersky experts only observed two minor updates in the payload part.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_26",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s2"
      },
      "text": "Conclusion It has been almost four years since Kaspersky first observed the Roaming Mantis campaign.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_27",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Roaming-Mantis-reaches-Europe(02-07-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s3"
      },
      "text": "Since then, the criminal group has continued its attack activities by using various malware families such as HEUR:Trojan-Dropper.AndroidOS.Wroba, and various attack methods such",
